# Shared Project State

Work on this repo runs in many parallel lanes. Context fragmentation — each agent holding a
private, drifting snapshot of the project — has caused more damage here than any code defect:
duplicated investigations, two lanes clobbering one file, and fixes re-broken by a sibling who
did not know they existed.

**Two files are the shared memory. Read both before forming a theory or editing anything.**

- `docs/process/M1-STATUS.md` — what is fixed (with the commit), what is open (with why it is
  deferred), what has already been **disproven**, the regressions and the guard now catching
  each, and what every gate is structurally blind to.
- `docs/process/LANES.md` — which lane owns which files, the standing rules, the environment
  quirks, and what counts as evidence.

## Rules

- **Check `M1-STATUS.md` before investigating.** Several hypotheses have already been tested
  and disproven with measurements. Re-deriving one wastes a lane; contradicting one without
  new evidence is worse.
- **Check `LANES.md` before editing.** Do not edit a file it assigns to another lane. If the
  honest fix needs one, stop and report what you need — do not work around it.
- **Write findings back.** Anything discovered that outlives your task — a defect you did not
  fix, a stale comment, a gate blind spot, an invariant nothing pins, a disproven theory —
  belongs in `M1-STATUS.md`, or in your report if you do not own that file. A finding only you
  know is a finding that will be rediscovered or lost.
- **Correct these files when they are wrong.** They are written by fallible agents. An audit
  already refuted a load-bearing claim in `M1-STATUS.md`; the correction was more valuable than
  the original. Say what you changed and why.
- **Prefer deleting stale state to appending.** These files are useful only while they are
  short enough to be read. Fold resolved detail into a line; delete what no longer informs a
  decision.

## Evidence standard

A claim in these files carries its evidence, or it carries an honest label saying it is
unverified. Do not launder a worker's report into a fact. "Merged" is not "works": a fix is
done when it is merged, gated, and recorded.
